title: YarnTest
---
Jack: Hey! This line comes from a <wave>Yarn file</wave> now.
ALPH: And effects still work, like <shake>shaking</shake> and <palette>colours</palette>.
Jack: TMP tags too: <b>bold</b>, <i>italic</i> and <u>underlined</u>.
ALPH: Colours: <color=red>named red</color>, <color=FF8800>hex orange</color> and <mark=FFFF0080>a highlight</mark>.
Mysterious Voice: Speakers without a character asset still get their name shown.
This line has no speaker, so the name box is empty.
<<jump YarnTest_Choices>>
===

title: YarnTest_Choices
---
<<declare $askedTwice = false>>
Jack: Now pick one. The choices should pop up as soon as this line finishes typing.
-> Tell me a joke.
    Jack: Why did the wizard fail his exam? He <shake>spelled</shake> everything wrong.
-> What's your name?
    Jack: It's Jack. It says so right there in the <wave>name box</wave>.
-> Ask again. <<if $askedTwice == false>>
    <<set $askedTwice to true>>
    Jack: Alright, once more. This option disappears next time.
    <<jump YarnTest_Choices>>
Jack: That's the end of the Yarn test. Choices work!
===
